    "schema_diff_summary": "layout.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Keep visual_row_count pub(crate). Change only the else if. The condition is one else if: else if scalar != '\\r' && scalar != '\\n' { width = width.saturating_add(1); }. Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not touch notice_from, visible_line_range, or span_line_window. The existing test a_carriage_return_has_no_width stays green. The test a_newline_has_no_width calls visual_row_count of ab, a newline, cd with columns 4 and tab width 4 and gets 1. ab, a carriage return, cd with columns 4 and tab width 4 stays 1. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines."
